From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:50:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 28/77] Fold Str(<int constant>, S) at -O3 only for string
 types without a code page

tcallnode.handle_compilerproc (in_str_x_string) rewrites Str(<const>, S)
as S := '<digits>' at level 3 for every destination; for an AnsiString
with a declared code page (AnsiString(866), UTF8String) the result then
had the constant's code page (0 for UTF8String) instead of the
destination's (tests/test/tcpstr14 fails at -O3). Upstream 9e4c8eac
removed the earlier encoding guard. Restrict the rewrite to ShortString,
WideString and UnicodeString.
---
 compiler/ncal.pas | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/compiler/ncal.pas b/compiler/ncal.pas
index 20678506..8854b116 100644
--- a/compiler/ncal.pas
+++ b/compiler/ncal.pas
@@ -2970,6 +2970,18 @@ implementation
                 begin
                   { Output variable }
                   outnode := para.left;
+
+                  { Assigning a string constant only does the same as the
+                    helper for these destinations: the ansistring helpers
+                    also set the code page passed in their extra parameter
+                    (the constant would get the source code page instead),
+                    and the chararray helpers leave the elements after the
+                    digits untouched (the assignment pads them with #0) }
+                  if not is_shortstring(outnode.resultdef) and
+                     not is_widestring(outnode.resultdef) and
+                     not is_unicodestring(outnode.resultdef) then
+                    exit;
+
                   para := GetParaFromIndex(paracount - 2);
 
                   if Assigned(para) then
